Z||000000||pHoOl||07-31-2001||12:27 AM||||Drove past the local rice hang out, and of course i had to talk $hit.  so they want me to race with my stock 88GT with their civic with NOS.  I didn't think there would be any way that i would win (especially since i have an auto) but it races a question of if it's possible.<P>My guess is that if he has NO2, there is no way i'd come close.  Am i right?  Also, for those of us with autos, how can we get a good launch when racing?  I know you can drop the trans out if you drop from neutral from too high of rpm.<P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||07-31-2001||12:40 AM||||Don't do a neutral drop!!  You destroy tranny's that way.  Power brake it.  Hold the brakes hard with your left foot while you bring the RPM's up to 2,000-2,500.<P>I'm sure you'll get him off the line, but he might get you up top.  NOS turns civic's from high 16(?) cars to high 15 cars.  Should be a decently even race.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||72vinman||07-31-2001||12:42 AM||||Go for it and let us know how you do. <BR>Throw some soy sauce on that ricer.||||reg||14
Z||000003||pHoOl||07-31-2001||12:45 AM||||I figured power braking would destroy the tranny too.  I just wonder if that's all that he has.  I know the other kid had headers and such.  something to bear in mind though..... thanks for the support.  Also, do you suggest manually shifting the auto?  if so, at what rpm?<P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||JayUSA77||07-31-2001||01:07 AM||||Listen to standard. he knows how to launch a auto, sticks are hard to launch without tire spin and or bogging the car.  N-E ways ive raced a SH!t load of ricers and if he has NITROUS then my guess is he has exhaust and a intake at least. One easy way to know if he has exhaust is the sound it gives off when driving. NOTHING is AS DISGUSTING as a ricer and his exhaust sound. and a intake is very vissible when they pop the hood as most of them or iodized the color of the car. if they have exhaust,intake,and nitrous they can run low 15's alllllll day. The best way to win is jump the line as much as possible. and im guessing that he has a stick so get him nervous and make him bog off the line.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||saleenfiero||07-31-2001||02:42 PM||||Someone said power braking wasn't alot better for your car than tranny dropping the damn thing, a while ago.  Is it okay to do it at 2000RPMs though? (not all the time, just when the situation calls for it)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||07-31-2001||02:51 PM||||Power braking is a lot better for the tranny than neutral drops.  Yes, power braking will heat up the tranny fluid.  But the only way I can see you really harming a tranny by power braking is if you hold it for 10 minutes.  <P>Neutral drops, on the other hand, have a tendancy to make various tranny parts fly out from underneath the car.  ||||reg||1
